ngterm: the formatter writes skipped cells unstyled (upstream agterm's zmx Ghostty patch, rebased onto
LIBGHOSTTY_VT_REV)

From upstream agterm v0.36.0 (https://github.com/umputun/agterm, MIT): scripts/zmx-patches/ghostty/
0001-formatter-unstyled-blanks.patch, the patch upstream applies to the Ghostty zmx links, whose snapshot a re-attach
replays. Rebased onto the pin's line numbers; the code is upstream's. Reason and remove-when:
build/patches/ghostty-vt/README.md.

src/terminal/formatter.zig: in HTML output, a cell with no text (one a program skipped with a cursor move) closes
the open style before it is buffered as a blank, so the spaces it becomes are written unstyled, where they were
written under the previous cell's style and a gap after a colored run came back painted. Cells the program wrote,
spaces included, keep their style; plain output is unchanged. The pin's fast cell-run path buffers blanks only under
the default style, so it needs no change. VT output is left as the pin writes it: since #14725 it steps over such
gaps with CUF (they come back unpainted) and restores background-only cells with ECH, which a style close before
them would undo. ngterm's HTML copy and write-file actions take it.

Applied by scripts/build-ghostty-vt.sh. No header changes.

--- a/src/terminal/formatter.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/formatter.zig
@@ -1433,6 +1433,7 @@
 
                     // Cells with no text are blank
                     if (!cell.hasText()) {
+                        try self.closeStyleForBlank(emit, writer, &style, &style_id);
                         blank_cells += 1;
                         continue;
                     }
@@ -2236,6 +2237,23 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /// closeStyleForBlank resets the style before a blank cell is buffered, so
+    /// HTML writes the buffered blanks unstyled. VT output steps over them
+    /// with CUF and restores background-only cells itself, so it is left as is.
+    fn closeStyleForBlank(
+        self: PageFormatter,
+        comptime emit: Format,
+        writer: *std.Io.Writer,
+        style: *Style,
+        style_id: *u32,
+    ) std.Io.Writer.Error!void {
+        if (comptime emit != .html) return;
+        if (style.default()) return;
+        try self.formatStyleClose(emit, writer);
+        style.* = .{};
+        style_id.* = 0;
+    }
+
     fn formatStyleClose(
         self: PageFormatter,
         comptime emit: Format,
